{"name":"Arresting Auburn","hex":"#5a3532","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arresting","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Striking, gripping."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of arrest"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arresting"},{"term":"auburn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark reddish-brown colour, often used to describe hair colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auburn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arrest","blocks":[{"text":"An arrest is the act of apprehending and taking a person into custody, usually because the person has been suspected of or observed committing a crime. After being taken into custody, the person can be questioned further or charged. An arrest is a procedure in a criminal justice system, sometimes it is also done after a court warrant for the arrest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/ICE.XCheckII.3cops1arrest.jpg/330px-ICE.XCheckII.3cops1arrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrest","wikidata":"Q1403016"},{"title":"Auburn hair","blocks":[{"text":"Auburn hair is a human hair color, a variety of red hair, most commonly described as reddish-brown in color. Auburn hair ranges in shades from medium to dark. It can be found with a wide array of skin tones and eye colors. The chemical pigments that cause the coloration of auburn hair are often pheomelanin with high levels of eumelanin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Uyghur-redhead.jpg/330px-Uyghur-redhead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn_hair","wikidata":"Q2419551"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Kidnappers_arrested_Rio.jpg/500px-Kidna